Palisade repository automation

Usage: cargo xtask <COMMAND>

Commands:
  adr                 The ADR tooling (docs/adr/PROCESS.md)
  audit               Run cargo-audit over the root and fuzz lockfiles, ignoring exactly the advisories deny.toml ignores
  ci                  Run the checks from .github/workflows/ci.yml locally
  bench-compare       Run every criterion bench at <commit> and at the working tree, and fail if a median is more than 10% slower outside the noise (bench.yml)
  check-commit-msg    Check a commit message file against Conventional Commits (the opt-in commit-msg hook in .githooks/ runs this)
  check-banned-terms  No commercial vendor or product names in any file or path (docs/banned-terms.txt, docs/NAMING.md)
  check-deps          Enforce the allowed dependency directions between crates
  check-fuzz-locks    Check that every crates/*/fuzz/Cargo.lock is current (cargo metadata --locked)
  check-testdata      Fail if any file in the repository that starts like an executable (MZ) is not allowlisted in testdata/manifest.txt
  check-manifests     Enforce workspace inheritance of package fields, lints and dependency versions, and that every crate README documents its features
  check-supply-chain  Enforce the duplicate-version budget, deny.toml ignore expiry and reasons, the cargo-vet criteria and exemption notes, and no audit.toml
  check-unsafe        Enforce the unsafe-code allowlist (unsafe-allowlist.txt, ADR 0011)
  dist                Release-build the Windows binaries (with --msi, the installer package) or the Linux server, with symbols and size reports, as CI does (docs/packaging.md)
  sign                Authenticode-sign and verify files (docs/releasing.md#code-signing)
  release             The release pipeline's steps (docs/releasing.md)
  docs                The documentation site (docs/ci.md#documentation-site)
  deps-report         Print the dependency report: duplicates, third-party crates per crate, third-party unsafe counts and code that runs at build time
  sbom                Reserved for the SBOM (#226); prints where it will be written and fails
  check-workflows     Enforce the CI runner and action policy for .github/workflows, and that nothing under .github names a cloud-managed build service
  threat-coverage     Check the threat model's tables, and that every test, fuzz target and CI check it cites exists (docs/security/threat-model.md)
  test-summary        Summarise a nextest JUnit report for the GitHub job page
  coverage-summary    Summarise a cargo-llvm-cov JSON summary for the GitHub job page
  coverage-gate       Fail if palisade-policy line coverage is lower than at <commit>; needs cargo-llvm-cov and cargo-nextest
  fixtures            Build the generated test fixture corpus into target/fixtures/
  golden              Check the corpus's hashes against testdata/golden/fixtures.txt
  fuzz                Build every cargo-fuzz target, seed it from the test fixtures and run it; needs the pinned nightly and cargo-fuzz
  help                Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help
